### Frontend

- Build accessible interfaces: semantic HTML, labeled controls, keyboard navigation, and visible focus states.
- Keep components small and colocate their styles, tests, and assets.
- Separate server state, client state, and derived state; avoid copying server data into local state.
- Route API access through a single client layer and handle loading, empty, and error states explicitly.
- Keep routing declarative and attach data requirements to the route that needs them.
- Avoid hardcoded user-facing strings when the project has a localization layer.
